learn-harness adapts the learning method of learnharness
(https://github.com/amosblomqvist/learnharness), copyright its authors,
licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0.

What is adapted: the theory in learnharness's docs/teaching-methodology.md
and the teacher, prober and practice prompts in src/agent/prompts/ (the
probe as binary search, the minimal tree, predict / teach / check, the
practice doctrine's modes, difficulty band and hint ladder, and the
graph-versus-ledger split). skills/learn-session/references/doctrine.md
restates these ideas in new, compressed wording. No learnharness code is
included. Some lists (the hint ladder rungs, the confidence-reading cases,
the three practice modes) keep the source's structure and labels.

The Field session type, the record templates and the setup skill are new
to this plugin.
